{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new utilities for concurrent iteration, statistical tracking, and set operations, alongside critical bug fixes and optimizations for existing functions. The public API must expose these changes with precise behavioral guarantees to ensure compatibility and correctness for downstream users.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m04",
      "text": "The `product_index` function must correctly compute the index of a given combination within the Cartesian product without relying on internal fillvalue heuristics."
    },
    {
      "id": "m05",
      "text": "The `iequals` function must strictly enforce that iterables have equal lengths before comparing their elements, raising an error or returning False if sizes differ."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "The `powerset_of_sets` function must return a tuple containing the original input set as its first element, in addition to all proper subsets."
    },
    {
      "id": "m13",
      "text": "The `exactly_n` function must handle negative integer inputs for `n` by returning False immediately, avoiding incorrect iteration or errors."
    },
    {
      "id": "m16",
      "text": "The `serialize` function must be exposed as a new public utility capable of converting iterable data into a standard Python list or tuple structure."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17",
      "text": "The `concurrent_tee` function must provide a thread-safe mechanism to split an iterator into multiple independent iterators simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "The `synchronized` decorator must be available to wrap callable objects, ensuring that their execution is mutually exclusive across threads."
    },
    {
      "id": "m19",
      "text": "The `extract` function must accept an optional `monotonic` argument that, when True, optimizes extraction by assuming the source iterable is sorted."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25",
      "text": "The `sized_iterator` wrapper must accurately report the length of the underlying iterable via the `len()` function, reflecting the total number of items it will yield."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27",
      "text": "The `gray_product` and `partial_product` functions must correctly handle cases where iterator arguments are exhausted or modified during iteration, preventing stale state issues."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28",
      "text": "The `running_mean` function must be exposed as a new recipe that yields the cumulative average of values from an input iterable up to each point."
    },
    {
      "id": "m29",
      "text": "Slicing a `numeric_range` object with a negative step must return an empty range if the start and stop parameters do not support backward traversal."
    },
    {
      "id": "m32",
      "text": "The `running_statistics` function must yield a `Stats` named tuple containing min, max, mean, and count values updated incrementally for each item in the input iterable."
    },
    {
      "id": "m34",
      "text": "All listed public names must maintain their existing signatures and behaviors consistent with version 11.0.0 standards, ensuring no regression in core itertools recipes."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that all new functions integrate seamlessly with the existing module namespace and that edge cases for concurrency and statistics are thoroughly validated."
}
